## Theorem

All three correction-direction source blocks admit exact recursive return in
the common B103 basis. Their target-by-source matrices have the following
certified data over `GF(11)`:

| source block | shape | nonzeros | rank |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| H20 | 1509 x 248 | 251,822 | 248 |
| H11 | 1509 x 1013 | 1,389,364 | 1013 |
| H02 | 1509 x 248 | 340,473 | 248 |

Concatenating these columns without reordering gives

```text
K_C in Mat_1509(GF(11)),
nnz(K_C) = 1,981,659.
```

The complete operator satisfies

```text
rank(K_C) = 1508,
det(K_C) = 0.
```

This rank statement has two independent exact witnesses:

1. the emitted normalized nonzero vector `r_C` satisfies `K_C r_C = 0`;
2. the emitted 1508-square minor has determinant `2 mod 11`.

Thus both the kernel and cokernel are one-dimensional. The independently
emitted normalized dual vector `ell_C` satisfies

```text
ell_C^T K_C = 0.
```

Embed the selected G3CC terminal source `b_C` in the final 248 H02 target
coordinates and set its H20 and H11 coordinates to zero. It has 229 nonzero
coordinates and obeys

```text
ell_C^T b_C = 2 mod 11.
```

Consequently `b_C` is not in `im(K_C)`. It spans the unique cokernel, and the
affine coefficient matrix

```text
K_tilde_C = [[K_C, b_C],
             [  0,   0]]
```

has rank 1509. This is an exact one-good-fiber obstruction certificate: the
selected source is not a redundant column that can be absorbed by solving
`K_C y = b_C` at this reduction.

## Proof certificate

The direct H20 and H11 source matrices independently reproduce the canonical
G3BK good-reduction hashes. Their coordinate solutions reconstruct the
ambient right-hand sides with zero residual through every retained lower-pole
stage; eight spread H11-to-H02 columns are independently reconstructed in the
largest chart. G3BQ supplies the hash-bound H02 block.

The verifier then reassembles `K_C`, checks both null identities, evaluates the
nonzero source pairing, and recomputes the determinant of the emitted
1508-square minor. These facts imply

```text
1508 <= rank(K_C) <= 1508
```

and the nonzero cokernel pairing implies

```text
rank([K_C | b_C]) = 1509.
```

## Interpretation and boundary

G3CD is the first point in this branch where the complete correction operator
and the independently selected normalized-delta source meet in one exact
finite object. Their meeting is nontrivial: the source detects precisely the
one missing image direction.

This theorem is deliberately restricted to the selected `GF(11)` terminal
fiber. A rank defect after reduction does not by itself prove that the
characteristic-zero operator has rank 1508; its determinant could be a
nonzero algebraic integer divisible by the selected prime. Nor does this
single-fiber obstruction prove source horizontality, integrate the G3BJ path,
construct an integral B89 marking, or decide the normal function or `beta_C`.

The next required object is a certified parameter-dependent atlas for
`K_C(a)` and `b_C(a)` along G3BJ, followed by the one selected rank-1510
inhomogeneous continuation and characteristic-zero/integral promotion.

